>
  <p class="lede">
    Lanternina invents an activity for an adolescent, has a parent approve it, and then runs it in
    a real room — on paper, on e-paper displays, and on physical buttons. It reads what comes back
    in handwriting, decides what happens next from that, and stops at an hour the parent set.
  </p>

  <p>
    A mini-PC in a house drives two e-paper displays, an inkjet and a flatbed scanner. Every
    page, reading and continuation request goes from the hub to the container API, which calls Foundry models. The house holds the clock and initiates requests. This describes local code checked on 7 September 2026; hardware and the deployed revision were not rechecked.
  </p>

