  <p>This example comes from the research notebook. The filled sheet is a synthetic proposal, not a verified solution. The reader recognized the written arrow and direction; the continuation asked for them to be revised after a new indication of the map's orientation.</p>

  <p>
    The reader describes added marks. The runner selects marks or blank; a degraded reading leaves it waiting. An <code>ask</code> branch sends the descriptions in the continuation prompt. The continuation is checked and screened, without a second parent approval or a repair.
  </p>

  <h2 id="memory">Memory</h2>
  <p>The system stores configuration, generated activities, endings, reported durations and reading-derived summaries. A separate call observes pages to calibrate load and writing; recent observations are used to compute the profile that steers prompts. The panel does not expose that profile as a score. The parent can clear activity memory and observations. A complete plain-language memory view is not built.</p>
  <p>The reading contract blocks implicit copying and pickling but permits the HTTP request body. An administrator can enable development retention for 14 days. Each retained reading has its own 14-day lifetime from writing. This exception is separate from ordinary observations used by the profile.</p>

  <h2>The stack</h2>

  <h3>In the house</h3>
  <p>
    Raspberry Pi Compute Module 5 on a PoE base board, Raspberry Pi OS. Two 7.5" e-paper displays on
    XIAO ESP32-S3, running a patched TRMNL firmware against our own BYOS server. Epson ET-2870 over
    IPP and eSCL, driverless. Frames 3D printed, units assembled by hand.
  </p>

  <h3>In the cloud</h3>
  <p>
    Microsoft Foundry in the EU for every language, vision and image call, behind a single router
    module that is the only place allowed to import a model SDK. Azure AI Content Safety on
    generation paths. The scan-reading route does not apply inbound-image Content Safety. Container Apps for the API, Cosmos DB, Blob
    Storage, Static Web Apps. Infrastructure as Bicep.
  </p>

